{id:'outbound',cat:'Sales Conversations',icon:'📞',title:'Build a Focused Outbound Block',time:8,level:'Foundation',summary:'Turn the weekly call standard into a ranked customer work block with a reason for every conversation.',why:'Activity produces more value when calls are prioritized by promise, risk, and opportunity.',triggers:['lowCalls','overdue'],objectives:['Rank overdue promises, risk accounts, dormant customers, and growth opportunities.','Use a customer-specific reason instead of “just checking in.”','Record the result and next follow-up before moving on.'],steps:['Start with overdue promises and customer-risk calls.','Move to dormant, declining, repeat-order, and expansion opportunities.','Use contact calls to deepen the account and reach decision-makers.','Protect two uninterrupted outbound blocks.'],script:'I’m calling with a specific reason. I was reviewing your past program and upcoming timing, and I want to make sure we plan the next need before it becomes tight. What is coming up that we should start on now?',objections:[['We do not need anything right now.','What month or event would make the next conversation useful so I can follow up at the right time?']],check:['20 customer calls plus 5 contact calls supports the 125-call weekly standard.','Document the result, promise, owner, and next date.'],quiz:'q-outbound',page:'action'},
{id:'discovery',cat:'Sales Conversations',icon:'🔎',title:'Discovery Before Recommendation',time:10,level:'Core Skill',summary:'Clarify audience, use, budget, quantity, decoration, timing, and approval before recommending products.',why:'Better discovery reduces revisions and makes the recommendation more credible.',triggers:['belowPace','lowAOV','assigned'],objectives:['Separate requirements from preferences.','Identify the actual in-hands date and approval path.','Recommend from evidence rather than sending a random product list.'],steps:['Who is the product for and how will it be used?','What quantity and budget range must work?','What visual feel and decoration are expected?','What is the actual in-hands date?','Who approves product, price, and art?'],script:'Before I narrow the options, can I ask a few quick questions so I recommend the right product instead of sending a random list?',objections:[['I just need pricing.','I can get pricing quickly. Quantity, garment use, decoration, and timing determine whether the number is meaningful, so let me confirm those first.']],check:['Audience','Use','Quantity','Budget','Decoration','Deadline','Decision-maker'],quiz:'q-discovery',page:'customers'},
{id:'next-step',cat:'Follow-Through',icon:'➡',title:'End Every Conversation With a Next Step',time:7,level:'Core Skill',summary:'Convert a useful conversation into a scheduled action with an owner, date, and success condition.',why:'Opportunities stall when both sides leave with a vague promise to reconnect.',triggers:['overdue','belowPace'],objectives:['Name the next action.','Assign the owner.','Choose the date before ending the conversation.'],steps:['Summarize what was decided.','State what you will deliver.','Confirm what the customer will review or approve.','Schedule the next conversation.'],script:'I’ll send the revised options by tomorrow at noon. Can we reconnect Friday morning after you have reviewed them?',objections:[['I will get back to you.','What day should I check back if I have not heard from you, so this does not get lost?']],check:['Action','Owner','Date','Success condition'],quiz:'q-followup',page:'action'},
{id:'dormant',cat:'Customer Growth',icon:'🌱',title:'Reactivate a Dormant Customer',time:9,level:'Growth',summary:'Reconnect with a valuable past customer using history, relevance, and a low-pressure next step.',why:'A dormant customer already knows the company; the goal is to learn what changed.',triggers:['dormant','growth'],objectives:['Reference the past relationship naturally.','Ask what changed in the buying pattern.','Secure a useful next step even without an immediate order.'],steps:['Review prior products, dates, and value.','Choose a seasonal, reorder, event, or planning reason.','Ask whether the need changed, moved, or went elsewhere.','Schedule the next useful contact.'],script:'I was reviewing the program we supported previously and realized it has been a while since we planned something together. Has the need changed, or is there something upcoming we should start thinking about?',objections:[['We are using someone else.','What mattered most in that change—price, timing, product selection, or service? I want to understand where we need to be better.']],check:['Past relationship','Reason now','What changed','Next date'],quiz:'q-growth',page:'customers'},
{id:'declining',cat:'Customer Growth',icon:'🛡',title:'Protect a Declining Account',time:10,level:'Growth',summary:'Use a relationship-reset conversation when the customer’s recorded activity is below the prior pattern.',why:'Decline can signal a changed program, lost contact, service frustration, or a missed opportunity.',triggers:['declining','retention'],objectives:['Discuss the change without accusation.','Identify service, contact, budget, or program changes.','Create a recovery or growth plan.'],steps:['Review the prior and current pattern.','Open with curiosity.','Ask what changed internally.','Own any service gap.','Agree on one next action.'],script:'I wanted to check in because your ordering pattern looks different this year. Has the program changed, or is there something we could be doing better to support you?',objections:[['Budget is tighter.','Let’s identify the programs that matter most and adjust product, quantity, or decoration without weakening the purpose.']],check:['Change observed','Curious question','Service check','Plan'],quiz:'q-growth',page:'customers'},
{id:'quote',cat:'Follow-Through',icon:'📄',title:'Quote Follow-Up That Advances the Decision',time:8,level:'Core Skill',summary:'Follow up with a decision question instead of asking only whether the customer received the quote.',why:'The strongest follow-up identifies what still needs to be solved.',triggers:['belowPace','overdue'],objectives:['Confirm the customer’s decision factor.','Surface the real obstacle.','Offer a revision or approval path.'],steps:['Reference the goal of the quote.','Ask whether the obstacle is product, price, timing, art, or approval.','Resolve one obstacle.','Schedule the next decision point.'],script:'Which part still needs to be solved before the program can move forward—product choice, budget, timing, or internal approval?',objections:[['It is still being reviewed.','What would make the review easier—a side-by-side recommendation, revised quantity, sample, or clearer timeline?']],check:['Decision factor','Obstacle','Revision','Decision date'],quiz:'q-followup',page:'orders'},
{id:'price',cat:'Objection Handling',icon:'💬',title:'Handle “Your Price Is Too High”',time:10,level:'Core Skill',summary:'Diagnose the concern before discounting and rebuild the recommendation around value and alternatives.',why:'Price can mean total budget, per-piece cost, unclear value, or an incomplete comparison.',triggers:['belowPace','lowAOV'],objectives:['Ask what the customer is comparing.','Protect the required outcome.','Offer intentional alternatives instead of automatic discounting.'],steps:['Acknowledge without defending.','Clarify total budget, per-piece price, or competitor comparison.','Confirm what cannot be sacrificed.','Adjust product, quantity, decoration, or structure deliberately.'],script:'Is the concern the total budget, the per-piece number, or how this compares with another option? Once I know that, I can adjust the right part without weakening what matters most.',objections:[['Another company is cheaper.','Can we compare the exact garment, decoration, quantities, fees, and timing? If the specifications are different, I can show where the value changes.']],check:['Clarify comparison','Protect requirements','Offer options','Confirm decision'],quiz:'q-objections',page:'customers'},
{id:'deadline',cat:'Production & Timing',icon:'⏱',title:'Manage a Hard In-Hands Date',time:9,level:'Operations',summary:'Work backward through inventory, art, production, and shipping before promising a firm date.',why:'A hard deadline requires every dependency to align.',triggers:['production','orderRisk'],objectives:['Confirm the true in-hands date.','Identify approval and shipping dependencies.','Avoid an unverified production promise.'],steps:['Ask what happens on the in-hands date.','Verify product inventory and substitutions.','Identify the art approval deadline.','Check the current production source.','Choose shipping based on the actual date.','Record the deadline prominently.'],script:'Because this date is firm, I want to work backward before I promise it. I need to verify inventory, art approval, production, and shipping, then I’ll give you the safest confirmed plan.',objections:[['I need you to guarantee it now.','I do not want to give you a confident answer that has not been verified. Let me confirm each dependency and return with the firmest available plan.']],check:['In-hands date','Inventory','Art deadline','Production','Shipping','Deadline documented'],quiz:'q-production',page:'production'},
{id:'update',cat:'Customer Service',icon:'📣',title:'Give a Proactive Order Update',time:7,level:'Service',summary:'Update the customer before they need to ask when an order is on hold, delayed, backordered, or linked to an issue.',why:'Customers judge communication as much as the problem itself.',triggers:['orderRisk','service'],objectives:['Verify the actual status.','Explain what is known and unknown.','Give the next update time.'],steps:['Review order, production, art, and backorder information.','State verified facts.','Own the next action.','Give a specific update time.'],script:'I wanted to give you an update before you had to ask. Here is what is confirmed, what I am still verifying, and when I will update you again.',objections:[['Why did nobody tell me sooner?','You should have received an earlier update. I’m taking ownership now, and I will keep the next communication time specific.']],check:['Verified facts','Unknowns','Owner','Next update time'],quiz:'q-service',page:'orders'},
{id:'art',cat:'Order Quality',icon:'🎨',title:'Art and Decoration Verification Checkpoint',time:9,level:'Operations',summary:'Verify logo, color, location, size, garment, and approval before the order reaches production.',why:'A short checkpoint prevents avoidable art-location, color, and completeness errors.',triggers:['art','repFault'],objectives:['Confirm decoration details against the customer request.','Check every location and garment group.','Make approval ownership clear.'],steps:['Match the logo file to the quoted decoration.','Confirm logo colors and thread or ink expectations.','Confirm every placement and size.','Verify garment color compatibility.','Confirm who approves the proof and by when.'],script:'Before I submit this, I want to read the decoration plan back exactly: logo, colors, location, size, garments, and approval contact. Please stop me if anything is different.',objections:[['It is the same as last time.','I’ll use the prior order as a reference, but I still want to verify the current garment, logo file, location, and colors.']],check:['Logo','Color','Location','Size','Garment','Approver'],quiz:'q-quality',page:'arterrors'},
{id:'documentation',cat:'Systems & Habits',icon:'📝',title:'Document the Interaction So the Next Step Survives',time:6,level:'Foundation',summary:'Write notes that preserve the customer need, result, promise, owner, and next date.',why:'Useful documentation protects the relationship when time passes or another person touches the account.',triggers:['overdue','lowCalls'],objectives:['Capture the result, not just “called.”','Record the customer need and objection.','State the next action and date.'],steps:['What happened?','What does the customer need?','What did the rep promise?','What happens next, by whom, and when?'],script:'Spoke with [contact]. Need [program] for [date]. Concern is [issue]. I will [action] by [date]. Follow up [date].',objections:[],check:['Contact','Need','Decision','Promise','Follow-up date'],quiz:'q-documentation',page:'action'},
{id:'decorations',cat:'Products & Decoration',icon:'🧵',title:'Match Decoration Method to the Program',time:10,level:'Product Skill',summary:'Compare screen print, embroidery, heat transfer, DTF, and sublimation based on garment, artwork, quantity, budget, and finished look.',why:'The right method protects both the visual goal and production reality.',triggers:['product','production'],objectives:['Explain primary use cases and tradeoffs.','Identify common artwork and garment limitations.','Verify current production before recommending from timing.'],steps:['Start with the desired visual result.','Confirm garment fabric and construction.','Review logo colors, detail, gradients, and size.','Consider quantity and durability.','Verify the current production source.'],script:'The best decoration method depends on the fabric, artwork detail, quantity, budget, and finished look. I’ll narrow it to the methods that protect all five.',objections:[['Which one is better?','Better depends on the garment, logo detail, quantity, budget, and the look you want. Let me show you the tradeoffs for this exact program.']],check:['Visual goal','Fabric','Detail','Quantity','Durability','Current production'],quiz:'q-products',page:'production'}
